, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4072, 'exposed': False}], 'notes': {'overview': {'id': 'overview', 'content': 'Pages 7-8 confirm taxonomy: reasoning, acting, interacting, with sub-categories (Fig 3); acting covers world models/VLA, robot/tools, assistants; interacting covers social capabilities, role-based interaction, open-ended societies. Page 13: Self-Consistency selects the most consistent answer among sampled reasoning paths (self-consistency sampling); Tree of Thoughts uses breadth-first and depth-first search controllers. Page 22: acting context - Say Can, Inner Monologue, Chain of Tools plan-execute-observe, Language-Driven Zero Shot Object Navigation.', 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-5803bf1c9a0002a5bd4f', 'ev-f5fa865a87a2cd077881', 'ev-4049593a30e2846f8394', 'ev-7f4d5e2fe0886c80c09b'], 'valid': True, 'request': 12}, 'reasoning': {'id': 'reasoning', 'content': 'Page 10: Self Consistency [Wang et al. 2022] is an ensemble that samples diverse reasoning paths, evaluates them, and selects the most consistent answer using majority voting (page 10 exact: \"selects the most consistent answer using majority voting\"). Tree of Thoughts [Yao et al. 2024]: page 13 states ToT introduces breadth-first and depth-first search controllers (two controllers). Page 13 quote on ToT search needed; page 9 Table 1 lists ToT depth-first-search prompts. Reasoning framing: CoT step-by-step (page 9), interpreter/debugger & planning & retrieval & evolutionary (pages 12-13).', 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-d2b420a2b23cdc8166d3', 'ev-419793694ae75f1e2b97'], 'valid': True, 'request': 13}}}\nLast output from code snippet:\nNone", "observations_images": null, "action_output": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 8226, "output_tokens": 32, "total_tokens": 8258}, "is_final_answer": false}}
