{"event": "section_note", "time": 1793247449.7329547, "run_id": "94c52558cc6343e88da198067bac3458", "seq": 245, "section": "reasoning", "pages": [16, 17, 18, 34, 36], "content": "Page 10: Self Consistency [Wang et al. 2022] samples diverse reasoning paths and \"selects the most consistent answer using majority voting\" (page 10). Tree of Thoughts [Yao et al. 2024]: page 13 introduces breadth-first and depth-first search controllers (two controllers). Pages 16-17: implicit reasoning via RL (DeepSeek-R1, GRPO, RLVR) vs explicit inference-time methods; memory gives experience/personality. Pages 17-18: retrieval augmentation (RAG, adaptive retrieval) adds timely info; DeepSeek-R1 with self-generated reasoning. Page 18: CoT step-by-step prompting; self reflection challenges: oscillating models and long traces overflow context, compress traces; System 1 vs System 2. Pages 34,36 (social/theory of mind): LLM chatbots vs 276 humans on social judgment; AucArena auctions on LLaMa2/Mistral/Mixtral/Gemini/GPT; Alympics water allocation strategy game. Keeps the two reasoning answers: majority voting; [breadth_first_search, depth_first_search]."}
